      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm going to piggyback here rather than creating a new feature request, because it's functionally similar.\n\nI think the nametag of the members of the group that owns an instance, while they are in that instance, should be highlighted in some way (with a small symbol or a color or something) regardless of whether the user is representing the group. This is a binary yes/no thing that has nothing to do with group graphics.\n\nIt would be extremely useful in larger groups to be able to tell at a glance if a user is new and should be welcomed and introduced to others.\n\nConversely visitors would know who to go to with questions or moderation requests.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-06-18T11:55:59.684Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# Issue: \n\nRight now there is no way for you to know if there actually is a member of the Group in the Group Instance you are joining.\n\nThis means that you might join a Group Public for example because you think that there would be people who moderate it in there, but it turns out that there is actually no member of that Group in there. Same thing goes for when you are trying to find other members of the Group you are in and so on.\n\n# Suggestion:\n\nShow how many Group Members are in a Group Instance, it could be done in a similar way to how you already show how many friends are in an instance.  \n\nThis would make it a lot easier to find other Members of a Group.",
